 and 'already' is temporally ambiguous.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-008\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Web servers have already replicated necessary content.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits the conditions and criteria determining which content must be replicated, the point in time by which replication must occur, and fallback behavior if content is missing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-009\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"are considered\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Are considered' is a weak, non-verifiable phrase that does not specify how traffic is handled, and 'anticipated' versus 'unanticipated' traffic are undefined.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-009\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Both anticipated and unanticipated user requests (traffic) are considered.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what concrete system actions or outcomes occur for anticipated versus unanticipated traffic, nor which component processes them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-010\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The format for service information description is defined\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Passive voice omits the actor or system component responsible for defining and using the format, and the format specification itself is neither provided nor referenced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-010\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The format for service information description is defined\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"PE-001\",\n        \"PE-002\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Exact duplicate of PE-001 and PE-002.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-011\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The format of service requirements is defined.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Passive voice omits the actor or system component responsible for defining and using the format, and the format specification itself is omitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-012\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Mediator-SR, mediator-PR, mediator-PA\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses undefined project-specific acronyms ('SR', 'PR', 'PA') whose referents are never defined anywhere in the document.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-012\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Mediator-SR, mediator-PR, mediator-PA interaction protocols are defined.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Passive voice omits who defines or implements these protocols, and the protocol specifications and error handling are not provided.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-012\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Mediator-SR, mediator-PR, mediator-PA\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"PE-003\",\n        \"PE-006\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Overlaps with PE-003 and PE-006 on the SR-mediator interaction protocol while using inconsistent naming order and capitalization ('Mediator-SR' and 'mediator-PR'/'mediator-PA' versus 'SR-mediator').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-013\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"works in conjunction with the PA\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Works in conjunction with' is imprecise and does not clarify the respective responsibilities of the Mediator and PA, and 'PA' is an undefined acronym.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Mediator works in conjunction with the PA to establish negotiation.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits the triggering conditions for negotiation, the specific steps and responsibilities of Mediator and PA, and error handling if negotiation cannot be established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-014\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"between PAs are identified\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the undefined acronym 'PAs' without a referent in the document, and 'are identified' is a weak phrase that does not clarify whether the protocols are formally defined or implemented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Interaction protocols between PAs are identified.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Passive voice omits who identifies or implements the protocols, and the protocol specifications themselves are missing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-015\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Malicious requests are identified and acted upon\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Both 'Malicious requests' and 'acted upon' are vague and imprecise, providing no clear definition of malicious traffic or the required action.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-015\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"identified and acted upon\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Fails to specify what concrete action or consequence occurs once a malicious request is identified, as well as the responsible component and detection criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Malicious requests are identified and acted upon.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"PE-007\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"PE-007 specifically requires malicious requests to be 'detected and rejected', whereas PE-015 restates the rule inconsistently as 'identified and acted upon', leaving open actions other than rejection and using inconsistent terminology.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-016\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"long-term\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Long-term' is a vague, subjective duration term without a defined boundary or timeframe.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-016\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"existing policies for long-term peering arrangement\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits a concrete duration and unit defining 'long-term', as well as the actual policy rules and the actors responsible for enforcing them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-017\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"short-term\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Short-term' is a vague, subjective duration term without a defined timeframe, and 'procedure' is unspecified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"PE-017\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"procedure to perform short-term negotiation\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits a concrete duration and unit defining 'short-term', as well as the negotiation procedure steps, responsible actors, triggers, and failure ha